Accident Detection System
Real-time traffic accident and anomaly detection from CCTV footage using YOLOv8 + LSTM.
Quick Start
bash# 1. Clone the repo
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd accident_detection

# 2. Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate   # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate

# 3. Run  setup
python setup.py

# 4. Fill in credentials
nano .env
Project Structure
accident_detection/
├── data/               # Datasets (gitignored)
├── models/             # Saved model weights
├── pipeline/           # OpenCV + inference code
├── alerts/             # SMS & email alert scripts
├── dashboard/          # Streamlit app
├── tests/              # Test scripts
├── logs/               # Incident logs
├── setup.py            # Day 1 setup script
├── requirements.txt    # Python dependencies
├── PLAN.md             # Project plan
└── .env                # Credentials (gitignored)
Dataset
Download UCF-Crime: https://www.crcv.ucf.edu/projects/real-world/
Tech Stack
YOLOv8 · OpenCV · TorchVision · LSTM · Streamlit · Twilio · Flask


How it works

CCTV Frame
    ↓
YOLOv8 → vehicles detected?  → Road accident pipeline
        → 5+ persons clustered? → Crowd/fight pipeline
    ↓
LSTM (per pipeline)
    ↓
Alert if anomaly_prob > threshold
 (train test split , some for the scripts)
